      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ubly incorporated on June 26, 1896, but settlers first opened a store in 1865, naming the settlement Pagett’s Corners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ubly,_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Pere Marquette Railroad depot, opened in 1898, became Ubly’s lifeline, shipping sugar beets, grain and dairy to Detroit and beyond.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ubly,_Michigan",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Built in 1907, the Citizens Bank Block also housed a harness shop and a library, making it a community hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubly%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The brick Ubly Schoolhouse, erected in the early 1900s, stands as a visible symbol of the town’s commitment to education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2025/08/31/history-of-ubly-michigan/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1914 the Ubly Loyal Orange Lodge marched in white shirts and hats, winning first prize at the countywide Orangemen’s celebration in Bad Axe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
